course: dictionary
lesson: 12681
title: What does distribution mean?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Distribution is a noun, and it has more than one meaning. Most often it means sharing things out among people or places. You can find its meaning by reading the words around it.
explain: «The teacher made a fair distribution of pencils, so every child had three.» The clues are fair, every child and had three. The pencils were shared out so that everyone got the same amount, so distribution means sharing out.
explain: Distribution can also mean how something is spread out over an area or a group. «The map shows the distribution of wild foxes across the country.» The map shows where the foxes are and how they are spread out.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence. «The teacher made a fair sharing out of pencils» still makes sense, so sharing out is a good meaning for distribution here.
fact: Distribution means the act of giving or sharing things out among people or places.
fact: Distribution can also mean the way something is spread out or arranged over an area or a group.
fact: In maths and statistics, a distribution shows how often each value or result happens in a set of data.
fact: In business, distribution means getting goods from factories to shops.
fact: Distribution is often used in phrases like «equal distribution», «food distribution» and «distribution of wealth».
exercise: «The teacher made a fair distribution of pencils, so every child had three.» What does distribution mean here? | Breaking the pencils into pieces | Counting the pencils that were lost | Writing the children's names on the pencils | *Sharing things out among the children
exercise: «The bar chart shows the distribution of test scores.» In maths, what does distribution show? | The name of the teacher who set the test | The colour of the chart | The day the test was held | *How often each score happens in the data
exercise: «The lorries carried the toys from the factory to the shops as part of the company's distribution.» In business, what does distribution mean? | Selling toys to children at home | Building new factories | Making toys by hand | *Getting goods from factories to shops
test: «The map shows the distribution of wild foxes across the country.» What does distribution show here? | *Where the foxes live and how they are spread out | How fast foxes can run | The number of foxes in one town only | The foxes' favourite food
test: When a teacher shares out prizes, which word is closest in meaning to distribution? | Breaking | Losing | *Sharing | Hiding
exam: Which sentence uses distribution to mean how something is spread out over an area? | «I ate my distribution at lunch.» | *«The distribution of frogs covers the whole pond.» | «The distribution is a red bus.» | «She has a distribution of blue hats.»
